<h3>Entropy-gated supervision (EGRSD)</h3>
<p>A further refinement is to weight the per-token divergence by the teacher's confidence — its entropy at that position. <strong>EGRSD</strong> integrates three signals: a reward-grounded direction (should this token be updated at all?), a teacher-student likelihood-ratio magnitude (how large is the divergence?), and a teacher-entropy confidence gate (is the teacher itself uncertain?).</p>
<p>The gate reduces supervision weight at high-entropy positions — positions where even the teacher, seeing the answer, assigns diffuse probability across many tokens. These positions are genuinely ambiguous (multiple valid next words exist), and forcing the student to mimic one particular distribution would suppress creative exploration. A nonzero floor ensures every token still contributes, avoiding dead zones in the gradient. On Qwen3-4B and Qwen3-8B, EGRSD advances the accuracy-length Pareto frontier beyond both GRPO and standard OPSD baselines.</p>
</section>

