<h3>Efficiency — diffusion LLMs</h3>
<p>d-OPSD applies on-policy self-distillation to diffusion language models, using suffix conditioning (the student learns from self-future-experience) rather than prefix conditioning. On four reasoning benchmarks, d-OPSD outperforms both SFT and RLVR baselines while needing only <strong>~10% of the optimization steps</strong> that RLVR requires — a 10× sample efficiency gain that makes it practical even on limited compute budgets.</p>

