<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: On-Policy Self-Distillation</h2>
    <p>On-Policy Self-Distillation, or OPSD, is a post-training framework where a single language model acts as both teacher and student simultaneously. The teacher role is given the correct answer to a question, while the student only sees the question itself. Both roles share the same model parameters. The student generates rollouts on-policy, and the teacher provides dense per-token KL divergence supervision over those exact rollouts — no external teacher model needed, no distribution mismatch between training and inference.</p>
    <p>Three prior approaches each fail at something. SFT trains on human tokens but infers on model tokens — a mismatch that compounds errors. RL provides on-policy training but assigns only one scalar reward to every token, making credit assignment difficult. On-Policy Distillation gives dense supervision but requires a separate, larger teacher that doubles GPU memory. OPSD combines the benefits of all three: on-policy training, dense per-token supervision, and no external teacher, while reducing GPU memory by 40 to 60 percent compared to standard OPD. The field has extended OPSD across eight design axes: hybrid RL plus self-distillation, feedback-driven methods using compiler errors or test failures, stability calibration via entropy gating, reasoning compression, cross-lingual capability transfer, vision and multimodal applications, structured trajectory segmentation, and foundational theory. Key results include: plus 8.85 points on safety alignment for R1-Distill 1.5B with OPSA, the best math reasoning Avg@16 across six benchmarks with DASD's direction-adaptive gating, and 10 times sample efficiency versus RLVR for diffusion language models with d-OPSD.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：在线自蒸馏</h2>
    <p>在线自蒸馏（OPSD）是一种大模型后训练框架，同一个模型同时充当教师和学生角色。教师角色能看到问题的正确答案，而学生角色只能看到问题本身。两个角色共享相同的模型参数。学生在线生成推理轨迹，教师在这些轨迹上提供逐词的KL散度监督信号，无需外部教师模型，也不存在训练和推理的分布不匹配问题。</p>
    <p>现有的三种方法各有缺陷：SFT用人类标注数据训练，推理时却用模型自己生成的词，产生曝光偏差；RL提供在线训练，但只为整个序列分配一个稀疏标量奖励，信用分配困难；在线蒸馏提供密集监督，但需要单独运行一个更强的教师模型，显存需求翻倍。OPSD融合三者优点，同时将显存降低40%至60%。在各领域的应用结果包括：OPSA在R1-Distill-1.5B上安全对齐提升8.85分；DASD在六项数学推理基准的宏平均Avg@16上达到最优；d-OPSD在扩散语言模型上的样本效率比RLVR高10倍。</p>
  </div>
